00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.280 align:start position:0%
meeting on February the 18th ministers  in charge of Europe's finances will take  stock of negotiations with the European  Parliament on the establishment of a  common mechanism for rescuing failing  banks in a drive to avoid any repetition  of taxpayer-funded bailouts the  so-called single resolution mechanism is  a key element of Europe's banking Union  and ministers are working hard to reach  an agreement with the European  Parliament before the end of the  parliaments current term in May the  European Central Bank will present to  the ministers its first quarterly report  on the implementation of the single  supervisory mechanism which was  established in October the council will  also discuss and most likely endorse the  Commission's annual growth survey which  asked member states to continue growth  friendly fiscal consolidation tackling  unemployment and modernizing public  administration as part of a set of  measures to continue correcting economic  imbalances and consolidate the incipient  economic recovery EU finance ministers  are also expected to set priorities for  the EU s budget for 2014 and adopt a  recommendation on the budget discharge  for 2012 setting a common position in  view of the forthcoming g20 finance  meeting is also on the agenda
 

